# Chroma library, modern Earth: bold ways, batch 1 (stage A, 2026-10-18).
# One bold way (sometimes two) per life event, and for each first bold way a well link and a badly link, each with its
# own bold way. Played only in played lives. Syntax: header of build.py.

# ================================================================ the club reaches the final

== bold: the club reaches the final / W
base: turn up early, kit ready, and do exactly the job you are given
likelier_if: has [keeping fit] +10; years [club member] 2 +5
- W | promise the coach to train every evening until the final, and play wherever you are put | v: conformity, achievement | act: promise the coach to train every evening until the final, and play wherever they are put | chance: 40 | grants: trophies won | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: {N} plays the whole final in the place nobody wanted, and comes home with a winner's medal.
works: The club lifts the cup, and {Ns} medal goes on the shelf at home, the first of its kind.
fails: The coach leaves {N} on the bench all day, and {N}, stung, stops going to the club at all.
fails: {N} trains until it hurts, the side loses anyway, and {N} gives up the club that summer.

== bold: the club reaches the final / U
base: study the other side's last five games, and share what you find with the coach
likelier_if: has [finding things out] +10; has [working with data] +5
- U | chart the other side's weak spots, and ask the coach to build the plan on them | v: achievement, self-direction | act: chart the other side's weak spots, and ask the coach to build the plan on them | chance: 35 | grants: mentor | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: The coach builds the whole plan on {Ns} notes, and after the final takes {N} under a wing.
works: The plan works, and from then on the coach teaches {N} the game, week by week.
fails: The coach takes the notes as a slight, and {N} is no longer welcome at the club.
fails: The plan falls apart in the first half, and the blame drives {N} out of the club.

== a place in the side
tier: link
of_bold: the club reaches the final / W
side: well
delay: 1-2
holds: trophies won
stages: all
age: 9-61
stakes: .6
tone: mixed
life: friends, play
horizon: weeks
roles: friend, the coach
earth: a season after the final, the old captain hangs up their boots and the side needs someone to lead it
scene: A season after the final, the old captain has hung up their boots. {friend} wants the armband, the coach has not chosen, and the whole side is waiting to see who steps up.
scene gone: {friend}, who played beside {N} in the final, has moved away. The coach has not chosen a new captain, and the side is waiting to see who steps up.
- W | back whoever the coach picks, and keep doing your own job | v: conformity | act: back whoever the coach picks, and keep doing their own job | chance: 85
- U | ask the coach what a captain needs, and work on that all winter | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 75
- B | tell the coach plainly that you want the armband | v: achievement, power | act: tell the coach plainly that they want the armband | chance: 70
- R | vote for your friend out loud, and cheer them out onto the pitch | v: benevolence, stimulation | act: vote for their friend out loud, and cheer them out onto the pitch | chance: 85
- G | ask the old members who should lead, and go with what they say | v: tradition | chance: 80
works: The side settles under its new captain, and the season starts well.
works: Whoever leads, the side pulls together, and {N} plays some of the best games of a lifetime.
fails: Two players fall out over the choice, and the side loses its first three games.
fails: The dressing room splits over it, and the season starts badly.

== bold: a place in the side / B
base: tell the coach plainly that you want the armband
likelier_if: has [public speaking] +10; years [on the team] 3 +5
- B | ask for the armband in front of the whole side, and promise them the cup | v: achievement, power | act: ask for the armband in front of the whole side, and promise them the cup | chance: 45 | requires: on the team | title: team captain | takes_if_fails: on the team
works: The side bangs the lockers in agreement, and the coach hands {N} the armband.
works: {N} leads the side out on the first day of the season, captain from then on.
fails: The side goes quiet, the coach gives the armband to someone else, and soon {N} loses the place in the side too.
fails: The promise sounds like bragging, and by spring {N} is off the team.

== the club without you
tier: link
of_bold: the club reaches the final / W
side: badly
delay: 1-2
stages: all
age: 9-91
stakes: .5
tone: mixed
life: friends, community, play
horizon: weeks
roles: friend, the old members
earth: a year after you walked away from the club, a friend there asks you to come and help on the open day
scene: A year after {N} walked away from the club, {friend} rings. It is the open day on Saturday, the old members are short of hands, and would {N} come?
scene gone: {friend} has moved away, but the old members still send {N} a card: the club's open day is on Saturday, and they are short of hands.
- W | go, and do whatever job they hand you | v: conformity, benevolence | act: go, and do whatever job they are handed | chance: 80
- U | go along and watch, and work out whether you still want it | v: self-direction | act: go along and watch, and work out whether they still want it | chance: 85
- B | say you will come if they make it worth your while | v: power | act: say they will come if it is made worth their while | chance: 75
- R | turn up in the old shirt, and act as if you never left | v: stimulation, hedonism | act: turn up in the old shirt, and act as if they never left | chance: 70
- G | sit with the old members at the tea urn, and hear the club's news | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 85
works: The open day goes well, and the clubhouse feels a little more like home again.
works: Old faces are pleased to see {N}, and nobody mentions the year away.
fails: The day is awkward, and {N} leaves early without saying goodbye.
fails: Too much has changed, and {N} feels like a visitor.

== bold: the club without you / G
base: sit with the old members at the tea urn, and hear the club's news
likelier_if: has [old comrades] +10; has [keeping fit] +5
- G | ask the old members for a fresh start, and a place back in the side | v: tradition, achievement | act: ask the old members for a fresh start, and a place back in the side | chance: 30 | title: on the team | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: The old members speak up for {N}, and the coach finds a place in the side again.
works: {N} is back in the club's shirt by the autumn, and plays as if the year away never happened.
fails: The coach says the side has moved on, and the hurt of it keeps {N} away from every other group {N} still belonged to.
fails: The ask goes badly in front of everyone, and {N} quits the one club {N} still went to.

# ================================================================ falling in love

== bold: falling in love / R
base: say the three words first, before your nerve fails
likelier_if: mark 'took a wild risk' +5; mark 'made a friend' +5
- R | tell them, in front of all your friends, that you are in love with them | v: stimulation, self-direction | act: declare their love in front of all their friends | chance: 35 | title: girlfriend or boyfriend | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: The room goes quiet, then {prospect} laughs and kisses {N}, and from that night they are a couple.
works: {prospect} says it back in front of everyone, and the two of them leave together, a couple.
fails: {prospect} says no, kindly, in front of everyone, and {N} cannot face the club where they all met again.
fails: The silence is terrible, and {N} gives up the group they all belong to rather than see those faces.

== bold: falling in love / U
base: ask them a long list of questions, to see whether you truly fit
likelier_if: has [calming people down] +10; mark 'owned up' +5
- U | tell them the plain truth about yourself, the worst first, and ask the same back | v: self-direction, benevolence | act: tell the new love the plain truth about themselves, the worst first, and ask the same back | chance: 35 | grants: friend for life | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: {prospect} hears all of it and answers in kind, and whatever comes of the romance, the two of them can tell each other anything for life.
works: The long honest night leaves {N} and {prospect} closer than most couples ever get, friends for good whatever happens.
fails: {prospect} repeats some of it to the crowd they share, and {N} cannot face that group again.
fails: The truth lands badly, the story goes round their friends, and {N} gives up the club where they all met.

== a year of being together
tier: link
of_bold: falling in love / R
side: well
delay: 2-3
holds: girlfriend or boyfriend
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 16-57
stakes: .7
tone: joy
life: love, family
horizon: months
roles: prospect, sibling, parent
earth: a year or two after you told someone you loved them in front of everyone, your family asks when the two of you will settle down
scene: {N} and {prospect} are still together, a year and more after that night. At {sibling}'s birthday, {parent} asks over the cake when the two of them mean to settle down.
scene gone: {prospect} has taken work in another town for a year, and they meet at weekends. At {sibling}'s birthday, everyone asks how long the two of them can keep it up.
- W | say plainly that you mean to stay together, and set no date yet | v: conformity, security | act: say plainly that they mean to stay together, and set no date yet | chance: 75
- U | talk it through with them first: money, home, children, all of it | v: self-direction, security | act: talk it through with the partner first: money, home, children, all of it | chance: 75
- B | say you will settle down when your own plans are in place | v: achievement, self-direction | act: say they will settle down when their own plans are in place | chance: 80
- R | laugh it off, and kiss them in front of the whole table | v: hedonism, stimulation | act: laugh it off, and kiss the partner in front of the whole table | chance: 85
- G | let it come in its own time, as it did for your parents | v: tradition | act: let it come in its own time, as it did for their parents | chance: 80
works: The question passes, and {N} and {prospect} walk home hand in hand.
works: Something is settled between them that night, even without a date.
fails: The question hangs over them for weeks, and they quarrel about it twice.
fails: {prospect} goes quiet on the way home, and {N} cannot tell why.
works gone: The question passes, and that weekend the two of them laugh about it on the phone.
works gone: Something is settled between them that night, even with the miles between.
fails gone: The question hangs over the weekends for a month, and they quarrel about it twice.
fails gone: The next call is short and quiet, and {N} cannot tell why.

== bold: a year of being together / W
base: say plainly that you mean to stay together, and set no date yet
likelier_if: years [girlfriend or boyfriend] 2 +10; has [family who will always take you in] +5
- W | ask them to marry you, there at the table, with the family to hear it | v: tradition, conformity | act: ask the partner to marry them, there at the table, with the family to hear it | chance: 40 | requires: girlfriend or boyfriend | title: engaged | drops_if_fails: kind:partner
works: {prospect} says yes before {N} has finished asking, and the whole table cheers.
works: The ring comes a month later, and the two of them are engaged from that night on.
fails: {prospect} says it is too soon, in front of everyone, and within weeks it is over between them.
fails: The silence at the table says it all, and {prospect} leaves {N} before the spring.
works gone: On the next weekend visit {N} asks, and the answer is yes before the question is finished.
works gone: The ring goes on at the station a month later, and the two of them are engaged from then on.
fails gone: The answer down the phone is that it is too soon, and within weeks it is over between them.
fails gone: The long silence on the line says it all, and the relationship ends before the spring.

